sid-133897606,imgsize-478419.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Bangladesh and India plan to resume train ops by October]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133896761.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/south-asia/bangladesh-and-india-plan-to-resume-train-ops-by-october/articleshow/133896761.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/south-asia/bangladesh-and-india-plan-to-resume-train-ops-by-october/articleshow/133896761.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-08T02:29:55+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Ahsan Tasnim</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133896788,imgsize-1156667.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Truth behind claim that Trump's H-1B fee plan could push cost above $200,000: Here's the calculation]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133896375.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/truth-behind-claim-that-trumps-h-1b-fee-plan-could-push-cost-above-200000-heres-the-calculation/articleshow/133896375.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/truth-behind-claim-that-trumps-h-1b-fee-plan-could-push-cost-above-200000-heres-the-calculation/articleshow/133896375.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-08T02:08:10+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Poulomi Ghosh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133896431,imgsize-829693.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[In 1876, Jesse James’s gang tried to rob a Minnesota bank for seven minutes; 150 years later...]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133895832.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In a dramatic seven-minute standoff in Northfield, Minnesota, local citizens bravely confronted the notorious James-Younger Gang during a bank heist, ultimately leading to the gang's capture. Today, the Northfield Historical Society preserves fascinating artifacts, including an outlaw's duster and even a mummified ear from that fateful day. The town now honors this brave moment in history with a lively annual festival.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1876-jesse-jamess-gang-tried-to-rob-a-minnesota-bank-for-seven-minutes-150-years-later-the-town-still-has-a-coat-a-saddle-and-an-outlaws-mummified-ear/articleshow/133895832.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1876-jesse-jamess-gang-tried-to-rob-a-minnesota-bank-for-seven-minutes-150-years-later-the-town-still-has-a-coat-a-saddle-and-an-outlaws-mummified-ear/articleshow/133895832.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-08T01:58:39+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133896325,imgsize-1306117.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[At 16, an Indiana girl earned 5 cents a day working at a café; her family later bought it]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133895345.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[South Bend's Sunny Italy Cafe, established in 1926, is celebrating its centennial anniversary.  This historic eatery has remained under family ownership for a full century.  The restaurant is renowned for its authentic, scratch-made Italian dishes and traditional recipes.  Generations of Notre Dame students and local residents have frequented the establishment.  Its enduring legacy highlights a unique culinary tradition in the community.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/at-16-an-indiana-girl-earned-5-cents-a-day-working-at-a-neighbourhood-caf-her-family-later-bought-it-and-100-years-after-it-opened-her-daughter-still-runs-it/articleshow/133895345.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/at-16-an-indiana-girl-earned-5-cents-a-day-working-at-a-neighbourhood-caf-her-family-later-bought-it-and-100-years-after-it-opened-her-daughter-still-runs-it/articleshow/133895345.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-08T01:24:31+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133895542,imgsize-1776689.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[67-year-old Colombian woman makes money selling neighbourhood gossip; she carries a notebook, collects evidence, also takes payment to keep her mouth shut]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133895251.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/67-year-old-colombian-woman-makes-money-selling-neighbourhood-gossip-she-carries-a-notebook-collects-evidence-also-takes-payment-to-keep-her-mouth-shut/articleshow/133895251.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/67-year-old-colombian-woman-makes-money-selling-neighbourhood-gossip-she-carries-a-notebook-collects-evidence-also-takes-payment-to-keep-her-mouth-shut/articleshow/133895251.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-08T01:07:30+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133895402,imgsize-82860.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[In 1952, Mary Tsingou programmed a Los Alamos experiment that helped change modern physics]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133893432.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In the 1950s, Mary Tsingou Menzel played a pivotal role in solving a complex physics problem using one of the earliest computers. Initially recognized only in a footnote for her computational work, her contributions to the Fermi-Pasta-Ulam problem have since gained fitting recognition. A true trailblazer in computational physics, she worked silently yet effectively in the realm of national security science.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/discovery/in-1952-mary-tsingou-programmed-a-los-alamos-experiment-that-helped-change-modern-physics-her-role-was-reduced-to-a-footnote-and-took-more-than-50-years-to-receive-proper-credit/articleshow/133893432.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/discovery/in-1952-mary-tsingou-programmed-a-los-alamos-experiment-that-helped-change-modern-physics-her-role-was-reduced-to-a-footnote-and-took-more-than-50-years-to-receive-proper-credit/articleshow/133893432.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-08T01:01:16+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133895368,imgsize-830286.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[What happened to Kal Dosanjh, Vancouver cop arrested for alleged fraud? His boss says, 'This officer had a profile in the community and internally, and officers are angry and disappointed']]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133893075.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/what-happened-to-kal-dosanjh-vancouver-cop-arrested-for-alleged-fraud-his-boss-says-this-officer-had-a-profile-in-the-community-and-internally-and-officers-are-angry-and-disappointed/articleshow/133893075.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/what-happened-to-kal-dosanjh-vancouver-cop-arrested-for-alleged-fraud-his-boss-says-this-officer-had-a-profile-in-the-community-and-internally-and-officers-are-angry-and-disappointed/articleshow/133893075.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-07T23:55:29+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Poulomi Ghosh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133893285,imgsize-53074.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Overdue Book Finally Returned: 1943 San Antonio loan arrives from Oregon; no late fee owed]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133862031.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[After 82 years, a library book borrowed in 1943 was finally returned in Oregon, revealing a heartfelt letter detailing its extensive journey. The family inquired about overdue fees, but fortunately, the library had abolished such fines in 2021. The book, still in excellent condition, was briefly showcased before being put up for sale.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-san-antonio-library-book-checked-out-in-1943-travelled-with-one-family-for-generations-82-years-later-it-came-back-from-oregon-with-a-note-about-the-late-fee/articleshow/133862031.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-san-antonio-library-book-checked-out-in-1943-travelled-with-one-family-for-generations-82-years-later-it-came-back-from-oregon-with-a-note-about-the-late-fee/articleshow/133862031.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-08T02:50:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133862121,imgsize-704027.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Paradise and Lahainaluna football teams unite after devastating wildfires]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133881322.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/californias-paradise-high-lost-its-town-to-fire-in-2018-and-lahainaluna-endured-the-lahaina-fire-in-2023-their-football-teams-have-now-met-in-hawaii-for-the-first-unity-bowl/articleshow/133881322.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/californias-paradise-high-lost-its-town-to-fire-in-2018-and-lahainaluna-endured-the-lahaina-fire-in-2023-their-football-teams-have-now-met-in-hawaii-for-the-first-unity-bowl/articleshow/133881322.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-08T01:50:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133881408,imgsize-878832.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Scientists tagged 14,000 endangered moths with paint and glue; none turned up, and that may be good news]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133863316.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In a groundbreaking study, researchers have tagged over 14,000 Bogong moths in the Snowy Mountains of Australia. However, after extensive tracking efforts, none have been recaptured, suggesting potential populations larger than previously assumed. Alternatively, these moths might be utilizing undiscovered migration routes. The ongoing project remains crucial for understanding the ecology of these endangered insects.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/scientists-tagged-14000-endangered-australian-moths-with-paint-and-eyelash-glue-to-trace-their-migration-not-one-was-found-and-researchers-say-that-may-be-good-news/articleshow/133863316.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/scientists-tagged-14000-endangered-australian-moths-with-paint-and-eyelash-glue-to-trace-their-migration-not-one-was-found-and-researchers-say-that-may-be-good-news/articleshow/133863316.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-08T01:48:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133863623,imgsize-2266165.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Scientists covered 200 square metres of a Swiss glacier with sheep’s wool; early tests found...]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133889880.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In an innovative approach, Swiss researchers are experimenting with natural wool blankets to mitigate glacier melting. These eco-friendly coverings have shown results comparable to synthetic options during trials. The initiative makes use of discarded sheep's wool, an agricultural byproduct. Although effective in localized regions, it's important to note that this technique alone won't reverse global warming—tackling greenhouse gas emissions is essential for the long-term preservation of glaciers.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/earth/scientists-covered-200-square-metres-of-a-swiss-glacier-with-sheeps-wool-early-tests-found-it-protected-the-ice-about-as-well-as-plastic-sheets-but-only-0-02-of-swiss-glacier-ice-is-covered/articleshow/133889880.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/earth/scientists-covered-200-square-metres-of-a-swiss-glacier-with-sheeps-wool-early-tests-found-it-protected-the-ice-about-as-well-as-plastic-sheets-but-only-0-02-of-swiss-glacier-ice-is-covered/articleshow/133889880.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-07T23:11:36+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133891970,imgsize-794813.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[An Australian woman learned she was pregnant and could give birth ‘any day’ within 24 hours]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133892027.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[An Australian mother was shocked to find out she was pregnant just days before giving birth to a very premature baby. Her daughter, Makerita Tanuvasa, entered the world at just 21 weeks and three days, weighing only 351 grams. Remarkably, she became Australia’s most premature surviving infant. After more than four months in intensive care, receiving specialized treatment, she finally returned home, marking a miraculous recovery.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/an-australian-woman-learned-she-was-pregnant-and-could-give-birth-any-day-within-24-hours-her-daughter-arrived-at-21-weeks-3-days-and-became-the-countrys-most-premature-baby-to-survive/articleshow/133892027.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/an-australian-woman-learned-she-was-pregnant-and-could-give-birth-any-day-within-24-hours-her-daughter-arrived-at-21-weeks-3-days-and-became-the-countrys-most-premature-baby-to-survive/articleshow/133892027.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-07T23:41:24+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133893134,imgsize-1128112.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Mooney M20F small plane crashes near Florida airport; pilot killed]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left